    "output_token_ids_sha256": "d25cbb2bc51898018beb20352e542131ec36cd24b90e02f456ffb3ebd0b5abb4",
    "raw_output": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Tuple, Optional\n\ndef reconcile_ledger(opening: int, entries: List[Tuple[int, int, int]]) -> Optional[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Reconciles a ledger by summing signed amounts.\n    \n    Args:\n        opening: Initial balance.\n        entries: List of (id, kind, amount) tuples.\n                 kind 1 = credit (positive), kind -1 = debit (negative).\n                 id must be unique across all entries.\n                 amount must be positive.\n    \n    Returns:\n        The reconciled balance or None if validation fails.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not entries:\n        return opening\n    \n    seen_ids: set[int] = set()\n    total: int = opening\n    \n    for id_val, kind, amount in entries:\n        # Validate id uniqueness\n        if id_val in seen_ids:\n            return None\n        \n        # Validate kind\n        if kind != 1 and kind != -1:\n            return None\n        \n        # Validate amount\n        if amount <= 0:\n            return None\n        \n        # Update state\n        seen_ids.add(id_val)\n        if kind == 1:\n            total += amount\n        else:\n            total -= amount\n            \n    return total\n```<|im_end|>",
